<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;">

		<tbody><tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">(1)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">This table is based upon information supplied by officers, directors and principal stockholders. Unless otherwise indicated in the footnotes to this table and subject to community property laws where applicable, we believe that each of the stockholders named in this table has sole voting and investment power with respect to the shares indicated as beneficially owned. Applicable percentages are based on 51,899,648&#160;shares outstanding on April 24, 2026, adjusted as required by rules promulgated by the SEC. The number of shares beneficially owned includes shares of common stock issuable pursuant to the exercise of stock options and warrants that are exercisable within 60 days of April 24, 2026. Shares issuable pursuant to the exercise of stock options and warrants vesting within 60 days of April 24, 2026, are deemed to be outstanding and beneficially owned by the person to whom such shares are issuable for the purpose of computing the percentage ownership of that person, but they are not treated as outstanding for the purpose of computing the percentage ownership of any other person.</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 8pt; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">(2)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">Consists of 9,090,909 shares of common stock held of record by CorMedix Inc. (&#8220;CorMedix&#8221;). The address for CorMedix is 300 Connell Drive, Suite 4200, Berkeley Heights, NJ 07922. Information regarding CorMedix, Inc. is based solely upon Schedule 13D filed with the SEC on September 12, 2025 by CorMedix, Inc.</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 8pt; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">(3)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">Consists of 4,661,502 shares of common stock. Excludes the right to purchase (i) 1,000,000 issuable upon exercise of warrants and (ii) 5,454,545 shares of common stock not currently purchasable due to beneficial ownership limitations on purchase. AIGH Capital Management, LLC (&#8220;AIGH CM&#8221;) is an advisor or sub-advisor with respect to the shares held by AIGH Investment Partners, L.P., and WVP Emerging Manager Onshors Fund, LLC - AIGH Series (collectively, the &#8220;AIGH Investors&#8221;), and may be deemed to have beneficial ownership of, and to control the voting and investment power of 4,661,502 shares of common stock held by the AIGH Investors. Each of AIGH Investment Partners, LLC ("AIGH LLC") and Mr. Orin Hirschman, as managing member of AIGH CM and president of AIGH LLC may also be deemed to have beneficial ownership of the shares of common stock. The address for each of AIGH CM, AIGH LLC and Mr. Hirschman is 6006 Berkeley Avenue, Baltimore, MD 21209. Information regarding AIGH Capital Management, LLC is based solely upon Schedule 13G/A filed with the SEC on January 30, 2026 by AIGH Capital Management, LLC.</p>
			</td>
		</tr>

</tbody></table>

