			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">(4)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">Consists of 4,266,211 shares of common stock issuable upon the exercise of pre-funded warrants. Nantahala Capital Management, LLC (&#8220;NCM&#8221;) is the investment advisor to certain private funds and managed accounts (the &#8220;NCM Investors&#8221;) that hold shares of common stock and certain derivative securities related thereto, including warrants. Each of Wilmot B. Harkey and Daniel Mack, the principals of NCM, may be deemed a beneficial owner of the warrants beneficially owned by NCM. Each of NCM, Mr. Harkey and Mr. Mack disclaims beneficial ownership of the warrants disclosed herein except to the extent of their respective pecuniary interests therein. Due to a beneficial ownership limitation, the number of shares of common stock reported excludes shares of common stock issuable upon exercise of pre-funded warrants, Series A common stock purchase warrants and Series B common stock purchase warrants held by the NCM Investors. These warrants are subject to a beneficial ownership limitation of 9.99%, which such limitation restricts the holder from exercising that portion of the warrants that would result in the holder and its related entities owning, after exercise, a number of shares of common stock in excess of the beneficial ownership limitation. The address for NCM and the NCM Investors is 130 Main Street 2nd Floor, New Canaan, CT 06840. regarding Nantahala Capital Management, LLC is based solely upon Form 4 filed with the SEC on March 17, 2026 by Nantahala Capital Management, LLC.</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 8pt; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">(5)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">Consists of 3,589,186 shares of common stock held directly by Rock Springs Capital Master Fund LP (&#8220;Master Fund&#8221;) and Four Pines Master Fund LP (&#8220;Four Pines&#8221;) and indirectly held by Rock Springs Capital Management LP (&#8220;RSCM&#8221;) and Rock Springs Capital LLC (&#8220;RSC&#8221;). RSCM serves as the investment manager to each of the Master Fund and Four Pines. RSC is the general partner of RSCM. Each of Mark Bussard and Kris Jenner may also be deemed to have beneficial ownership of the shares of common stock. Due to a beneficial ownership limitation, the number of shares of common stock reported excludes shares of common stock issuable upon exercise of purchase warrants held by Master Fund and its affiliated entities. These warrants are subject to a beneficial ownership limitation of 9.99%, which such limitation restricts the holder from exercising that portion of the warrants that would result in the holder and its related entities owning, after exercise, a number of shares of common stock in excess of the beneficial ownership limitation. The address of the entities and individuals referenced in this footnote is 650 South Exeter, Suite 1070, Baltimore, MD 21202. Information regarding Rock Springs Capital Management LP is based solely upon Schedule 13G filed with the SEC on September 12, 2025 by Rock Springs Capital Management LP.</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 8pt; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">(6)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 8pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">Consists of 3,579,273 shares of common stock held of record by Rosalind Master Fund L.P. (&#8220;RMF&#8221;). Excludes 9,571,681 shares issuable upon the exercise of pre-funded warrants and warrants because they contain a blocker provision under which the holder thereof does not have the right to exercise any of the warrant to the extent that such exercise would result in beneficial ownership by the holder in excess of 9.99% of the common stock. Consequently, as of April 24, 2026, RMF was not able to exercise any of the warrants due to the blockers. Rosalind Advisors Inc. (&#8220;Advisor&#8221;) is the investment advisor to RMF and may be deemed to be the beneficial owner of shares held by RMF. Steven Salamon is the portfolio manager of Advisor and may be deemed to be the beneficial owner of shares held by RMF. Gilad Aharon is the portfolio manager and member of Advisor and may be deemed to be the beneficial owner of shares held by RMF. Notwithstanding the foregoing, each of Advisor, Mr. Salamon, and Mr. Aharon disclaims beneficial ownership of the shares. The address for Advisor, Mr. Salamon and Mr. Aharon is 15 Wellesley Street West, Suite 326, Toronto, Ontario M4Y 0G7 Canada. The address for RMF is P.O. Box 309, Ugland House, Grand Cayman, KY1-1104, Cayman Islands. Information regarding Rosalind Master Fund L.P. is based solely upon Schedule 13G/A filed with the SEC on February 11, 2026 by Rosalind Advisors, Inc.</p>
			</td>
		</tr>
